---
description: Enforce next-intl APIs; forbid direct i18n JSON imports outside i18n bootstrap
alwaysApply: false
---

# next-intl is mandatory for translations

Never import translation catalogs directly from `@/i18n/**/*.json` in app, components, hooks, services, repositories, queries, actions, route handlers, or utilities.

Use next-intl APIs instead:

- Client components (`"use client"`): `useTranslations("<namespace>")`
- Server contexts (`"use server"`, async RSC, server actions, route handlers, metadata): `await getTranslations("<namespace>")` or `await getTranslations({locale, namespace})`

This includes logs and fallback messages. Do not read messages from raw JSON in runtime code.

Exception (allowed): i18n bootstrap/config files that assemble catalogs (e.g. `i18n/request.ts`).

```ts
// BAD
import dbMessages from "@/i18n/db/es.json"
console.error(dbMessages.db.pages.failed_to_fetch)

// GOOD (server)
import { getTranslations } from "next-intl/server"
const t = await getTranslations("db")
console.error(t("pages.failed_to_fetch"))
```
